## Title: Daseeki Bags
## Notes: A standalone bag interface for WoW Classic Era.
## Author: Daseeki
## Category: Bags & Inventory
## X-License: MIT
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1592410
## OptionalDeps: Daseeki-Core
## Interface: 11507, 11508, 11509
## Version: 2.0.0
## SavedVariables: DaseekiBags2DB, DaseekiBags2Data
##
## Daseeki-Bags 2.0 — clean rewrite. This v2.toc documents the intended 2.0
## load order for the fresh flat tree; it is NOT wired into the live addon yet
## (the shipping Daseeki-Bags.toc still loads the 1.x tree). Cutover in a later
## wave replaces Daseeki-Bags.toc with this file and deletes the 1.x sources.
##
## New SavedVariables (additive; coexist with the 1.x globals
## DaseekiBagsAccount / DaseekiBagsSets / DaseekiBagsMesh, which 2.0 reads
## READ-ONLY once at first load via migrate.lua and never writes):
##   DaseekiBags2DB   — settings (schema-versioned)
##   DaseekiBags2Data — inventory cache DB (owners graph; per-container identity)
##
core.lua
store.lua
capture.lua
migrate.lua
# --- W2 (UI) --- loads after Daseeki-Core (OptionalDeps) so DaseekiUI exists ---
borders.lua
ui_items.lua
ui_frame.lua
# --- W3 (bank / owner selector / offline views / cross-char find) ---
# ui_owner: shared owner-selector flyout (consumes ns.Frame view state)
# ui_bank:  the bank window (consumes ns.Items grid, ns.Owner, ns.Sort)
ui_owner.lua
ui_bank.lua
# --- W4 (search / sort / options / features) --- pure engines + DaseekiUI page ---
search.lua
# rules2: simplified custom-categories engine (a category = a saved search query;
# reuses the search.lua matcher). Consumed by ui_frame (combined-view sections)
# and options.lua (the editor). Loads after search.lua (its matcher) so the
# self-tests can exercise the delegated grammar.
rules2.lua
sort.lua
# ui_find: cross-character Find window (consumes ns.Search matcher, ns.Frame/ns.Bank)
ui_find.lua
options.lua
# features.lua: tooltip cross-char counts, event auto-display, Alt-click flash-find
# (self-wires on the core bus; consumes ns.Store / ns.Frame / ns.Search surfaces).
features.lua
#
# Bindings.xml is deliberately NOT listed here. The client auto-discovers
# Bindings.xml at the addon root and hands it to the KEYBINDINGS parser. Listing
# it as a .toc file entry ALSO feeds it to the generic UI-XML parser, which does
# not know the <Binding> element -- that is what produced the LUA_WARNINGs the
# owner saw on every load ("Unrecognized XML: Binding", "Unrecognized XML
# attribute: header/category"). No shipping Era addon lists Bindings.xml in its
# .toc, and 1.x never did either. Do not re-add it.
#
# Load order is irrelevant for the auto-loaded file: each <Binding> body runs
# only on keypress, and every body is guarded on its handler global existing.
